claim.claim-text:
1. A method, comprising:
generating a first emulsion using: (i) a first aqueous fluid comprising a reagent, and (ii) a partitioning fluid comprising a fluorinated oil and a fluorosurfactant comprising a perfluoropolyether (PFPE), wherein the first emulsion comprises a first plurality of droplets dispersed in the partitioning fluid, wherein a first droplet of the first plurality of droplets comprises the reagent at a first concentration;
generating a second emulsion using: (i) a second aqueous fluid comprising a plurality of cells and a plurality of beads, wherein a bead of the plurality of beads comprises a plurality of nucleic acid barcode molecules, and (ii) the partitioning fluid, wherein the second emulsion comprises a second plurality of droplets dispersed in the partitioning fluid, wherein a second droplet of the second plurality of droplets comprises a cell of the plurality of cells and the bead of the plurality of beads, and wherein the reagent is absent from the second droplet or present in the second droplet at a second concentration that is lower than the first concentration;
contacting the first emulsion with the second emulsion; and
transferring the reagent from the first droplet to the second droplet via an aggregate of surfactant molecules comprising the reagent.
